"""Q53 r3b: replace Q53 matched/core/classification/verdict entries in /output/report.json with the fixed-window + uv-test + MC versions (out/q53/*)."""
import json
R=json.load(open('/output/report.json')); res=R['results']
drop=('Q53: matched-beam','Q53: core-scale','Q53: classification','Q53: verdict')
res[:]=[x for x in res if not str(x.get('quantity','')).startswith(drop)]
CONV=("T_B (RJ) integral over ONE fixed common velocity window (N 2785, S 2750 km/s, +-350 km/s, same for both lines and J; linear baseline from 450-950 km/s; noise from line-free channels incl. baseline term; Gaussian fits abandoned: the lines are double-horned) at the fixed N/S position, pbcor cubes convolved channel-wise to ONE common circular beam per value; 1\"=188 pc. 3-2: 2017.1.00379.S Xb4b (0.3-1.9\") and Xb4d (>=1.1\"); 4-3: HCN 2018.1.00493.S X1df1 spw29 (native 0.87x0.69\"), HCO+ 2018.1.00223.S X858 spw27 (native 0.39x0.35\"), smallest common beam 1.0\". Errors shown are statistical; systematics in the MC entry (flux scale 10% per project, missing flux, pointing, window).")
EV="scripts/q53g_fixedwin_all.py -> out/q53/fixedwin_all.csv; q53e_fixedwin43.py -> fixedwin43.csv, posoff43.csv, spec43.npz; q53f_plotspec.py -> spec43_overlay.png; q53h_mc.py -> mc.json"
def add(q,v,unit='',conf='medium',unc='',extra=()):
    res.append(dict(quantity=q,value=v,confidence=conf,evidence=EV,target='N, S',uncertainty=unc,unit=unit,assumptions=[dict(name='conventions',value=CONV)]+list(extra)))
add("Q53: matched-beam HCN/HCO+ 3-2 and 4-3 (T_B, fixed velocity window) at N and S, one circular beam per value",
 "3-2: 0.3\" (56 pc) N 0.98+-0.03 / S 0.49+-0.02; 1.0\" (188 pc) 0.84+-0.01 / 0.40+-0.01; 1.9\" (357 pc) 0.72+-0.01 / 0.37+-0.01 (Xb4b; Xb4d at 1.1\" 0.84/0.40, at 1.9\" 0.74/0.39). 4-3: 1.0\" (188 pc) N 0.81+-0.02 (stat) / S 0.22+-0.02; 1.4\" 0.73/0.19; 1.9\" (357 pc) 0.67/0.18; 2.5\" (470 pc) 0.62/0.17. Earlier Gaussian-fit values (N 0.70, S 0.22 at 1.0\") underestimated N (HCO+ Gaussian +13%). N/S contrast: 3-2 2.0 (56 pc), 2.1 (188 pc), 2.0 (357 pc); 4-3 3.7 (188 pc), 3.7 (357 pc) (3.3 at 188 pc after the missing-flux correction). 4-3 ratio at 1.0\" at the line-peak position equals the fixed-position value (N 0.81, S 0.22; HCO+ peak N at 0.2\" W: 0.79); rms over +-0.2\" offsets 0.02 (N), 0.016 (S). N-S separation 5.1\": Gaussian cross-contamination <1e-4.",
 'ratio',conf='high',unc='statistical as quoted (+-0.01-0.03); full budget (10%/project flux scale, missing flux, pointing, window) in the MC entry: N 4-3 at 188 pc 0.80 (0.69-0.93, 16-84%), S 0.23 (0.18-0.29)')
add("Q53: uv/missing-flux test of the 4-3 ratio (new X1df1 and X858 cubes vs same-project Xb47 4.1x2.7\" cubes, all at 4.5\" circular)",
 "At 4.5\": N HCN 4-3 7.5 vs Xb47 8.6 K km/s (new cubes recover 88%), N HCO+ 12.8 vs 16.7 (77%); S HCN 2.5 vs 4.2 (61%), S HCO+ 11.4 vs 13.1 (87%). Ratio at 4.5\": N 0.59 (new) vs 0.52 (Xb47); S 0.22 vs 0.32. The two new projects therefore miss extended emission, HCN at S most. Adding the missing flux as a smooth additive DeltaT_B (N: +1.1 HCN, +3.9 HCO+; S: +1.6, +1.8 K km/s) to the 1.0\" values changes the ratio N 0.81->0.79, S 0.22->0.24 (<=7%): the 188 pc ratios are not driven by uv coverage, but a component structured on 1-4\" would not be captured by this test. No visibilities of the two 4-3 projects were re-imaged. 3-2 uv check: Xb4b vs Xb4d at 1.1\"/1.4\": N 0.836/0.835, S 0.395/0.402 (1.0 vs 1.1\"); at 1.9\" N 0.72/0.74, S 0.365/0.388.",
 'ratio',unc='+-0.02 (N), +-0.015 (S) stat on each; smooth-component assumption not verified',conf='medium')
add("Q53: S HCN vs HCO+ 4-3 line shape (25 km/s centroid and 120 vs 192 km/s width mismatch)",
 "Both lines are double-horned at both nuclei (spec43_overlay.png), not Gaussian. At S HCO+ shows blue (~2710) and red (~2830 km/s) horns of similar strength; HCN is dominated by the blue horn. Ratio by half-window at 1.0\" (split at 2780 km/s): S blue 0.27, red 0.13; N blue 0.82, red 0.81. The Gaussian fit to HCN locks on the blue horn (centroid 2718) while HCO+ fits the blend (2743): the mismatch is a spatial/kinematic component with weak HCN (red horn, ratio 0.13), not a vibrational HCN (v2=1 is 1480 km/s away), absorption or H13CN blend. The S ratio depends on the window/baseline (HW 250-450 km/s: 0.14-0.24; 0.22 at the adopted HW 350), always <0.30. 3-2 behaves alike (S blue 0.40, red 0.39 at 1.0\"; red 0.60 at 0.3\", noisy).",
 'ratio',unc='S 0.22 +0.02/-0.08 for window/baseline choice')
add("Q53: R43/R32 versus beam and the core (56 pc) 4-3 ratio",
 "R43/R32 (fixed window, matched beams) N: 0.97, 0.95, 0.93, 0.89 at 1.0, 1.4, 1.9, 2.5\"; S: 0.56, 0.50, 0.49, 0.45: NOT beam-independent; it rises toward small beams in both nuclei (weighted linear slope -0.053/\" N, -0.064/\" S; partly a missing-flux effect of the 4-3 cubes at larger beams, so the slope is an upper bound). Core 4-3 (0.3\") = R32(0.3\") x R43/R32 with flat..linear-trend extrapolation: N 0.95 (16-84%: 0.81-1.12), S 0.29 (0.25-0.35). RADEX (radex_ratio.json, tau10~5-12) gives N 0.7-1.0, S 0.27-0.39: consistent. Earlier 'N 0.88' used a constant ratio-of-ratios 0.84 from Gaussian fits and is superseded. 1-0 values quoted elsewhere (N 0.96/0.94, S 0.645/0.60) are Harada+2018 Table 13 (1.7\") and Michiyama+2018 Table 4 (2.1\") in out/q53/lit_table.csv, not measured here.",
 'ratio',unc='as in 16-84% ranges (stat + 10%/project flux scale + missing flux + extrapolation model)')
add("Q53: classification of N and S in the Izumi+2016 4-3 ranges (SB 0.24-1.03, median 0.48; AGN 1.11-3.19, median 2.6) by Monte Carlo",
 "MC (200000 draws; stat Gaussian; flux scale lognormal 10% per project (HCN and HCO+ from different projects => 14% on ratio); missing-flux factor Gaussian centred half-way to the corrected value with sigma half the correction; pointing Gaussian rms of the 0.2\" offset grid; window-choice sigma from HW 250-450; core: 3-2 0.3\" ratio x R43/R32 uniform between flat and linear-trend extrapolation, 5% 3-2 relative scale, 5% pointing). N at 188 pc (4-3 0.80, 0.69-0.93): P(<=1.03)=0.95, P(>=1.11)=0.014, P(gap)=0.03: SB-like. N core 56 pc (0.95, 0.81-1.12): P(<=1.03)=0.68, P(>=1.11)=0.18, P(gap)=0.15: the 4-3 diagnostic is NOT discriminating at the N core (value sits at the top of the SB range, 2x SB median, and P(AGN-like)=0.18 > 0.1), while at >=188 pc (and 0.62-0.81 up to 470 pc) N is clearly SB-like. The 3-2 N core (0.98+-0.03 at 56 pc) is likewise inside the literature ULIRG 3-2 peak range (Imanishi+2019 median 1.3, 16-84% 1.0-1.85) but at its low edge. S at 188 pc (0.23, 0.18-0.29) and core (0.29, 0.25-0.35): P(<=1.03)=1.0, P(<=0.48, the SB median)=1.0: S is below the SB median and 9x below the AGN median at every beam 56-470 pc; the submm 'HCN enhancement' diagnostic fails at S (false negative). S AGN class is X-ray based, Compton-thick and energetically minor.",
 'probability',unc='conditional on the stated input distributions; extrapolation model (flat vs linear R43/R32) moves the N core median 0.93-0.97')
add("Q53: verdict on HCN/HCO+ as AGN diagnostic in NGC 3256",
 "(1) S (AGN) is below SB values at 1-0 (0.60-0.65, 1.7-2.1\" literature), 3-2 (0.37-0.49) and 4-3 (0.17-0.29): false negative, measured at 56-470 pc. (2) N is SB-like at 4-3 at >=188 pc (0.62-0.81); at the N core the 4-3 diagnostic is not discriminating (P(SB range)=0.68, P(AGN-like)=0.18). The 3-2 N core 0.98 is inside the ULIRG range, a beam-dependent 'false positive' that vanishes at 357 pc (0.72). (3) The N/S contrast persists at 357 pc (3-2 2.0, 4-3 3.7), so it is not only a core effect. (4) Q47: tau10(HCN)~5-12 at both nuclei and X_S/X_N unconstrained (median ~1, 95% 0.45-2.6), so HCN/HCO+ is not an abundance measure and an XDR enhancement at S is untested (needs H13CN/H13CO+). Consistent with Harada+2018, Privon+2017.",
 '',unc='see MC entry')
json.dump(R,open('/output/report.json','w'),indent=1)
print(len(res))
